+# M5-03 implementation and evaluation handoff
+
+Status: **BLOCKED for task completion; available-host evaluation delivered for review.** Date: 2026-10-06. Review base `75f1038c48f7b5c9afbbba91fef837d2a7794506`; prerequisite M4-01 `f7d2a93eabae724f29875a29840b000cee8749fb`. The coordinator alone owns completion checkboxes and the shared ledger.
+
+The authoritative result, versions, checksums, exact fixture commands, platform limits and setup corrections are in [java-import.md](java-import.md). That report distinguishes native import failures from successful Gradle-derived shadow adaptation. It makes no production support claim.
+
+## Delivered scope and requirement mapping
+
+| Required assertion / task step                                                               | Implementation or evidence                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | Result                                                                    |
+| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| M5-03.1 reproducible evaluation; canonical runtime pins                                      | `packages/core/src/ftc/java/language-service.ts` consumes canonical `FtcEnvironment.Profile` artifact subset and explicit paths; `m5-03.test.ts` verifies local pins then runs actual candidate. `prepare.py`, `pathing.py`, `classpath.init.gradle`, `shadow.py`, `probe.py` preserve the rerun procedure | Delivered, not registered                                                 |
+| M5-03.2 / EDT-01 / ENV-04: real FTC, Android, generated and pathing import                   | Three actual, compiling FTC 11.1 projects with Gradle 8.9 / AGP 8.7.0 and explicit Java 17; JDT LS 1.46.1 on Java 21. Native files were outside JDT's classpath                                                                                                                                            | FAIL for native import; Windows NOT RUN                                   |
+| Completion, expected definition, clean semantic diagnostics and deliberate-error diagnostics | Actual LSP requests/responses in `m5-03/*-result.json`; assertion rejects syntax-only fallback and checks definition URI provenance                                                                                                                                                                        | PASS for all five domain samples in Gradle-derived shadows on macOS arm64 |
+| Generated sources are real                                                                   | AGP-generated FtcRobotController BuildConfig, successful real compiler task, original/copy/hash records in `*-provenance.json`, definition into `generated/.../BuildConfig.java`                                                                                                                           | PASS on adapted macOS fixtures                                            |
+| M5-03.3 exact harness command                                                                | Real `M503_CONFIG=... bun test ./test/ftc-evaluation/m5-03.test.ts`, native and shadow modes separately retained                                                                                                                                                                                           | Native fails honestly; shadows pass; missing real config skips            |
+| Failure, cancellation and cleanup                                                            | Real TERM-resistant inherited-pipe descendants exercised on exit, AbortSignal and timeout. Per-run process group cleanup and separate owned Gradle `--stop`; post-run process check                                                                                                                        | PASS on macOS; Windows process ownership unverified                       |
+| No import-time I/O or production enabling                                                    | Source only exports a pure launch recipe; runtime process code stays under test fixtures. No imports into composition/registration, manifests, lockfiles or shared schema changes                                                                                                                          | Preserved                                                                 |
+| M5-03.4 decision and remaining failures                                                      | `java-import.md` decision, observed matrix, provenance, limitations                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | Recorded; no supported catalog promotion                                  |
+| M5-03.5 review/commit / AC-04                                                                | Scoped checks below and independent review handoff; full editor/Windows/production isolation absent                                                                                                                                                                                                        | Review pending; task/AC remain open                                       |
+
+The separate local path object is intentionally an evaluation input; M4-02's production local toolchain descriptor is not implemented here. The launcher does not discover Java through PATH. It validates canonical artifacts, minimum Java 21 editor compatibility, numeric build-runtime identity and explicit absolute paths; Gradle is configured with the separate build runtime. No Effect service or production subprocess binding is introduced before the gate is satisfied.
+
+## Verification commands and exact results
