+Counts differ between probe runs because runtime-validation and cleanup regression tests were added during the evaluation. Logs preserve observed output (trailing whitespace normalized) instead of relabeling earlier runs. No artificial failing test was created for observed third-party compatibility; new launcher, cleanup and cursor behavior followed RED→GREEN. Actual LSP observations use real binaries and dependencies; only source samples, bad member edits and process-tree adversaries are fixtures.
+
+The covering suite initially failed two existing local HTTP/WebSocket tests under the filesystem/network sandbox (`EADDRINUSE` on ephemeral loopback bind). Authorized rerun outside that sandbox passed. No unrelated source changes were made. The known Schema event-manifest/App locale baseline failures were outside this task's changed packages/selection and were not repaired. No Session/timeline code was changed; no performance claim is made.
+
+## Ownership, retained assets and limitations
+
+User projects, the installed Android Studio runtime, installed SDK, Gradle cache and original source archive were read or copied. Native upstream preservation was checked against all 110 files. The pathing fixture changes were restricted to one selected dependency in each copied TeamCode build. No robot/controller endpoints, deployment, start, tuning or production command registration were used.
+
+The AGP provisioning incident and exact existing license-state digests are documented in `java-import.md`. Existing installed platform-tools stayed 35.0.1; only the owned SDK received 37.0.1. Later imports/build commands disable SDK auto-download. JDK executable hashes are not complete distribution hashes, and no unsupported production profile is asserted.
+
+At the coordinator's explicit request, **`/private/tmp/m5-03-tools` is retained through independent review and follow-on tasks**. It contains pinned downloads, copied SDK/cache, three owned native fixtures, three shadow projects, setup inputs and JSON configs needed for exact reruns. The coordinator owns later targeted cleanup. Per-run `m503-lsp-*` directories and Python bytecode scratch were removed. No owned JDT/Python or Gradle daemon remained at the final process inspection. The harness stops only its own Gradle user home; it does not stop the user's IDE/Gradle services.
+
+Remaining completion blockers: Windows host/process-tree evidence; failing native Android import or an approved, fully integrated classpath adapter; complete production runtime-package provenance; M9-07/M9-08 production isolation. Packaged editor, offline network isolation, broad pathing/tuning API coverage, performance/resource minima and source attachment navigation are not established by this task's sampled host evaluation. Shared checklist and supported catalog remain unchanged by this worker.
